Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-yaml, python3-apt, postgresql-common, curl
Recommends: maludb-mc2dbd, postgresql-18-maludb-core
Description: MaluOS first-boot provisioning and the maluctl tool
 On the first boot of a MaluOS system, maluos-firstboot.service creates
 the MaluDB database with the maludb_core extension, a tenant schema
 (enable_memory_schema), an administrator principal, PostgreSQL roles
 for the MC2DB listener and for the operator users, generates the
 listener bearer token and starts the listener. Configuration comes
 from /etc/maluos/firstboot.yaml, which cloud-init user-data may write.
 .
 maluctl shows status, prints or rotates the listener token, manages
 principals and re-runs provisioning idempotently. `maluctl update` reports
 and applies software updates (unattended-upgrades policy, apt).
